# MechaHarness requirements (for host / consumer application code)

Copy into your project's `.cursor/rules/` (or equivalent) when the app depends
on MechaHarness.

- Prefer `from mechaharness.host_apis import …` for authority, denial,
  isolation, recipe lifecycle, correlators, and host_kit helpers.
- Wire with `MechaHarnessConfig` hooks + constructor injection; do not grow
  `Settings` with lane-only knobs or hand-construct harness families.
- Product recipe promotion: `promote_recipe` (policy + held-out gate + hooks),
  not ungated `registry.promote`.
- Open identity: host types are classes / namespaced strings — do not patch
  closed library enums to add a host concept.
- Events: keep OBS correlators (`graph_id`, `recipe_id`/`recipe_version`,
  `authorization_epoch`, nest `parent_run_id`); no secrets in payloads;
  warehouse/UI joins live in the host.
- Durable denial stores, campaign UIs, and warehouse ETL are host-owned.

